\ GAME-OV ------- OVERLAY PREFIX -------------------            \ QUIT                                                          VOCABULARY GAME IMMEDIATE                                       120 OPEN-OVERLAY                                                GAME DEFINITIONS                                                6 width !                                                       1870 TRANS-ALLOT ( allot space for heads)                                                                                       NEWT-DP                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ CONSTANTS                                                                                                                     136 FILE-START @ 64 / C: SAVBLK \ offset in starflit.a          SAVBLK  0 + C: KRNBLK \ base block for kernal image             SAVBLK 51 + C: DSPBLK \ base block for display image            SAVBLK 67 + C: RTNBLK \ base block for return stack image       SAVBLK 68 + C: PRMBLK \ base block for parameter stack          SAVBLK 69 + C: ARRBLK \ base block for array data                4 C: RDROP  \ # bytes to drop from the return stack             0 C: SDROP  \ # bytes to drop from the parm stack              16384 C: 16K                                                    1024  C: 1K                                                     ' NOP C: KERNSAVESTART \ start offset above which is saved                                                                                                                                      cr blk ? ." t-dp " t-dp @ u. ." here " here u.                  \ VARIABLES                                                                                                                     V: RESUME           \ resume play flag                          V: RTNTEMP 220 ALLOT \ temp return stack space                  V: NSYSK            \ new memory size in k bytes                V: CKSUM            \ check sum accumulator                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ VARIABLES                                                     V: LMARG       \ left margin                                    V: RMARG       \ right margin                                   V: TMARG       \ top margin                                     V: BMARG       \ bottom margin                                  V: CHARHEIGHT  \ height of character                            V: CHARWIDTH   \ width  of character                            V: LINESPACING \ pixels between lines                           V: CPL         \ characters/line                                V: LPS         \ lines/screen                                   V: $ADDR       \ string address                                 V: $LEN        \ length of string                               V: #LINES      \ number of lines string occupies                V: SUB$ADDR    \ substring address                              V: SUB$LEN     \ substring length                               V: TIMEKEY-VAL \ value of key pressed at pause or key           \ VARIABLES                                                     EXIT                                                            0 c: stsp \ start splash image                                  v: pauses 500 pauses !                                          v: #l/brs  v: #b/brs                                            v: brush-size 512 brush-size ! \ = for current moons            V: BRUSHBLK \ block offset of brushes within starflit.a         v: yoffset v: xoffset                                           v: keyprest                                                     v: bseg                                                                                                                         head: @SEG T:  bseg @ T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ TABLES                                                                                                                         9 C: HOST-ENTRIES  \ # of entries in HOST table                18 C: #VECTORS      \ # of entries in VECTORS table             TABLE HOST \ table of host environment parameter pointers          SYSK      , MAXDRV   , #CACHE  , [#CACHE] ,                     DBUF-SEG  , HBUF-SEG , BUF-CNT , MONITOR  , ' mps ,                                                                          TABLE VECTORS \ table of selected execution vectors                COLOR     , DCOLOR   , ABLT    , WBLT     , LBLT    ,           XORMODE   , XBLT     , YBLT    , YTABL    , ASKMOUNT ,          ' EMIT @ ME + ,   ' TYPE @ ME + ,  'VERSIONERR ,                TIME ,  TIME 2+ , LAST-UPDATE , LAST-UPDATE 2+ ,                BLTSEG ,                                                                                                                                                                                     \ COLORPFA PCCOLOR TACOLOR                                      exit                                                            TABLE COLORPFA \ storage addresses associated w/ colors 0-15      ' BLACK , ' DK-GREEN , ' DK-BLUE , ' LT-BLUE ,                  ' RED ,   ' GREY2 ,    ' VIOLET ,  ' BLUE ,                     ' BROWN , ' GREEN ,    ' GREY1  ,  ' LT-GREEN ,                 ' ORANGE , ' YELLOW ,  ' PINK ,    ' WHITE ,                                                                                  V: PCCOLOR -2 DP +! \ pixel bit patterns for regular PC           0 C, 1 C, 2 C, 3 C, 4 C, 5 C, 6 C, 7 C, 8 C, 9 C, 10 C,         11 C, 12 C, 13 C, 14 C, 15 C,                                                                                                 V: TACOLOR -2 DP +! \ pixel bit patterns for regular Tandy        0 C, 1 C, 2 C, 7 C, 8 C, 5 C, 14 C, 6 C, 12 C, 3 C, 10 C,       11 C, 13 C,  9 C, 12 C, 15 C,                                                                                                 \ trgb  tcomp                                                                                                                   v: trgb -2 dp +! \ tandy rgb pallete constants                     0 c, 2 c, 1 c, 11 c, 4 c, 8 c, 5 c, 9 c,                        6 c, 10 c, 7 c, 3 c, 12 c, 14 c, 13 c, 15 c,                 exit use above for composite also                               v: tcomp -2 dp +! \ tandy composite pallete constants              0 c, 1 c, 2 c, 6 c, 12 c, 5 c, 13 c, 6 c,                       12 c, 3 c, 10 c, 11 c, 13 c, 9 c, 12 c, 15 c,                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ ?TANDY set.tandy.pallete                                                                                                      HEX                                                             HEAD: ?TANDY ( -- t )                                           \ Is this a Tandy 1000 machine?                                 T: F000 C000 LC@ 21 = T;                                                                                                        head: set.tandy.pallete ( pfa -- )                              \ Set tandy color pallete registers given address of pallete    \ table.                                                        t: 10 0 do 10 i + 3da p! i over + c@ 3de p! loop                   drop  3 3da p! t;                                            decimal                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ SET.COLORS                                                                                                                    HEAD: SET.COLORS ( -- )                                         \ Set colors based on machine.                                  T: ?TANDY IF ( ?tandrgb @)                                                   ( if) trgb                                                      ( else tcomp )                                                  ( then)                                                         set.tandy.pallete                                            then t;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \ test tandy colors                                             exit                                                            : .bar ( x y ) 10 0 do 2dup i + over 40 + over lline loop         2drop ;                                                       : .colors 16 0 do i dup 16 * + !color                                             10 dup i * .bar loop ;                        : gtest                                                           set.colors >display >lores dark .colors key drop >alpha ;                                                                     : rtest ?tandrgb on gtest ;                                     : ctest ?tandrgb off gtest ;                                    : 10tests 10 0 do rtest ctest loop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ INIT$PTR APPEND$                                                                                                                                                                              V: $PTR V: $LEN                                                 HEAD: INIT$PTR ( addr -- ) T: $PTR ! $LEN OFF T;                HEAD: APPEND$  ( addr cnt -- )                                  T: $PTR @ $LEN @ + SWAP DUP $LEN +! CMOVE T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ !$ #CPL #LPS                                                                                                                  HEAD: !$ ( addr cnt -- \ set current string)                    T: $LEN ! $ADDR ! T;                                                                                                            HEAD: #CPL ( -- \ compute characters/line)                      T: RMARG @ LMARG @ - CHARWIDTH @ / CPL ! T;                                                                                     HEAD: #LPS ( -- \ compute lines/screen)                         T: TMARG @ BMARG @ - CHARHEIGHT @ LINESPACING @ + / LPS ! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ ?BL<-                                                                                                                         HEAD: ?BL<- ( addr -- addr' \ given address, end if space else) T: ( decrement until a blank space is encountered)                BEGIN                                                             DUP C@ BL = NOT                                               WHILE                                                             1-                                                            REPEAT T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ ##LINES                                                                                                                       HEAD: ##LINES ( -- \ compute number of lines will be occupied)  T: ( by the current string)                                       $ADDR @ SUB$ADDR !                                              1 #LINES !                  ( count initialized)                BEGIN                                                             SUB$ADDR @ CPL @ + DUP                                          $ADDR @ $LEN @ + U<                                           WHILE                                                             ?BL<-                     ( address.of.linebreak.blank --)      1+ SUB$ADDR !                                                   1 #LINES +!                                                   REPEAT DROP T;                                                                                                                                                                                \ #YBLT #XBLT .SUB$                                                                                                             HEAD: #YBLT ( -- \ compute initial line location for current )  T: ( text message so that the message is centered)                ##LINES                                                         LPS @ #LINES @ - 2/ CHARHEIGHT @ LINESPACING @ + * NEGATE       TMARG @ + YBLT ! T;                                                                                                           HEAD: #XBLT ( -- \ compute x location for current substring)    T: ( such that the current substring is centered)                 YBLT @ 900 YBLT ! 0 XBLT ! SUB$ADDR @ SUB$LEN @ TYPE            YBLT ! RMARG @ LMARG @ + 2/                                     XBLT @ 2/ NEGATE + XBLT ! T;                                                                                                  HEAD: .SUB$ ( -- \ plot centered substring)                     T: #XBLT SUB$ADDR @ SUB$LEN @ TYPE T;                           \ .#LINES                                                       HEAD: .#LINES ( -- \ plot current string as center formated)    T: #YBLT                                                          $ADDR @ SUB$ADDR !                                              BEGIN                                                             SUB$ADDR @ CPL @ + DUP                                          $ADDR @ $LEN @ + U<                                           WHILE                                                             ?BL<-                     ( address.of.linebreak.blank --)      SUB$ADDR @ -                                                    SUB$LEN ! .SUB$                                                 CHARHEIGHT @ LINESPACING @ + NEGATE YBLT +!                     SUB$LEN @ 1+ SUB$ADDR +!                                      REPEAT DROP                                                     $ADDR @ $LEN @ + SUB$ADDR @ - SUB$LEN ! .SUB$ T;                                                                              \ .FORMAT BORDERMARGINS                                                                                                         HEAD: .FORMAT ( addr count -- \ plot center formated string)    T: !$ #CPL #LPS                                                    .#LINES T;                                                                                                                   HEAD: BORDERMARGINS                                             T: 20 LMARG ! 140 RMARG !                                          40 BMARG ! 150 TMARG !                                          3 LINESPACING !                                                 9 CHARHEIGHT !  6 CHARWIDTH ! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \ ERASEWIND ERASELINE .PAGE                                                                                                     HEAD: ERASEWIND ( -- \ erase text in display window)            T: COLOR @ 150 20 40 150                                                         ( 140) BLACK POLY-WINDOW-FILL !COLOR T;                                                                        HEAD: ERASELINE ( -- \ erase text below display window)         T: COLOR @ 17 20 5 159 BLACK POLY-WINDOW-FILL !COLOR T;                                                                         HEAD: .PAGE                                                     T: BORDERMARGINS ERASEWIND >2FONT .FORMAT T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ BORDER                                                                                                                        HEAD: BORDER ( -- \ display standard interface border with )    T:  ( Interstel logo)                                             WHITE !COLOR                                                      5 155  10 160 LLINE  10 160 150 160 LLINE                     150 160 155 155 LLINE 155 155 155  25 LLINE                     155  25 150  20 LLINE 150  20  20  20 LLINE                      20  20  17  23 LLINE  17  23  17  30 LLINE                      17  30  14  33 LLINE  14  33   8  33 LLINE                       8  33   5  36 LLINE   5  36   5 155 LLINE                       5  29 COLOR @ .1LOGO T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ PRESSANY .GAMEOPS                                                                                                             HEAD: PRESSANY ( -- \ display message below border)             T: >2FONT 20 17 POS. ERASELINE                                     ." PRESS ANY KEY TO CONTINUE" >0FONT KEY DROP T;                                                                             HEAD: .GAMEOPS  ( -- \ display message below border)            T: >DISPLAY DARK BORDER beepoff                                    >3FONT 46 171 POS. ." GAME" 10 XBLT +! ." OPTIONS"              >2FONT 39  17 POS. ." SELECT AN OPTION"                                34 120 POS. ." 1. SAVE GAME"                                    34 100 POS. ." 2. RESUME GAME"                                  34  80 POS. ." 3. CHANGE DISPLAY MODE"                          34  55 POS. ." 9. END GAME" >0FONT T;                                                                                                                                                 \ .SAVEHEAD .LOADHEAD                                                                                                           HEAD: .SAVEHEAD ( -- \ display save game header message)        T: >3FONT 53 171 POS. ." SAVE" 10 XBLT +! ." GAME" >0FONT T;                                                                    HEAD: .LOADHEAD ( -- \ display load game header message)        T: >3FONT 53 171 POS. ." LOAD" 10 XBLT +! ." GAME" >0FONT T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ PRESSEXIT  INIT$PTR APPEND$                                                                                                   HEAD: PRESSEXIT ( -- \ display message below border)            T: >2FONT 30 17 POS. ERASELINE                                     ." PRESS ANY KEY TO EXIT" >0FONT KEY DROP PAGE BYE T;                                                                        EXIT                                                            V: $PTR V: $LEN                                                 HEAD: INIT$PTR ( addr -- ) T: $PTR ! $LEN OFF T;                HEAD: APPEND$  ( addr cnt -- )                                  T: $PTR @ $LEN @ + SWAP DUP $LEN +! CMOVE T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ TIMEKEY                                                                                                                       HEAD: TIMEKEY ( d -- )                                          \ Wait for d ms or until a key is pressed.                      T:  TIME D@ D+                                                    BEGIN TIME D@ 2OVER D>                                                'KEY DUP TIMEKEY-VAL !                                    OR UNTIL 2DROP T;                                                                                                             HEAD: TS! T: TIMESTAMP ! T;                                     HEAD: TS@ T: TIMESTAMP @ T;                                                                                                     HEAD: :TS! T: DUP :TIMESTAMP ! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \ !TIMESTAMP TME>FILE                                                                                                           HEAD: STS \ SET.TIME.STAMP                                      T: ( -- \ take the lo word of the real time clock)                 ( and store it into the variable TIMESTAMP; 0 not allowed)      TIME 2+ @ ?DUP 0= IF 2 THEN TS! T;                                                                                           \ HEAD: TME>FILE ( -- \ write the timestamp to the current file)\ NOTE: virgin play disk has 0 in timestamp field.              \ T: TS@ :TIMESTAMP ! SAVE-BUFFERS                              \   CLOSE OPEN 2DROP T;   \ update DOS directory date & time                                                                    HEAD: NTS \ NEW.TIME.STAMP                                      T: TS@ STS TS@ SWAP TS!                                            MOUNTA :TS! MOUNTB :TS! ts! t;                                                                                               \ [ASKMOUNT]                                                                                                                    HEAD: [ASKMOUNT] ( -- )                                         \ Request user to mount disk with file on drive specified       \ in current FCB.                                               T: PAD 50 + INIT$PTR dark BORDER                                   " PLACE DISK CONTAINING FILE " APPEND$                          NAM 8 -TRAILING APPEND$                                         ASCII . PAD C!  TYP PAD 1+ 3 CMOVE                              PAD 4 APPEND$                                                   "  INTO " APPEND$                                               DRV C@ ?DUP IF " DRIVE " PAD SWAP CMOVE ASCII @ +                              PAD 7 + C! PAD 7                                             ELSE " ANY DRIVE" THEN                              APPEND$                                                         $PTR @ $LEN @ .PAGE PRESSANY T;                              \ [VERSIONERROR]                                                                                                                HEAD: [VERSIONERROR] ( addr ct -- )                             \ Warn user if correct file not loaded.                         T: PAD 50 + INIT$PTR dark BORDER                                   " PLACE DISK CONTAINING THE CORRECT " APPEND$                   APPEND$ "  FILE" APPEND$                                        $PTR @ $LEN @ .PAGE PRESSANY T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \ .CKSUMERROR  SAVECHK                                                                                                          HEAD: .CKSUMERROR ( -- \ warn user of checksum error)           T: ERASELINE BEEP                                                  " SAVED GAME INTEGRITY ERROR." .PAGE PRESSEXIT T;                                                                            HEAD: SAVECHK ( -- \ warn user game not saved)                  T: :SAVE @ NOT                                                     IF ERASELINE BEEP                                                  " GAME IN PROGRESS BUT NOT SAVED." .PAGE                        PRESSEXIT                                                    THEN T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ ?-writable nomaster                                                                                                           head: ?-writable ( -- t )                                       \ Determine if current file is not writable.                    t:  255 derror !                                                  @ds pad 50 +  dta 2!  dos-dta                                   0 relrec !   1 recsize !                                        read-random                                                     write-random 2drop init                                         derror @ 0= t;                                                                                                                head: nomaster ( -- )                                           t: ctinit " MUST PLAY ON A WRITABLE COPY." .tty                    " PRESS ANY KEY TO EXIT." .tty key drop bye t;                                                                                                                                               \ GRAPHIC.DOS.ERRORS                                                                                                            HEAD: GDE \ GRAPHIC.DOS.ERRORS                                  T: ' <CTASKMOUNT> ASKMOUNT !                                       ' <CTVERSIONERROR> 'VERSIONERR ! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \ .RESUMING OUTERSPACE ?2SWAP                                                                                                   HEAD: .RESUMING  ( -- \ display press key to resume message)    T: " RESUMING THE GAME IN PROGRESS..." .PAGE 1000 MS T;                                                                         HEAD: OUTERSPACE ( -- seg )                                     \ 1st seg of outerspace.                                        T: @DS 4096 + T;                                                                                                                HEAD: ?2SWAP ( d d' t -- d' d or d d' )                         T: IF 2SWAP THEN T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \ PRESERVEDISPLAY RESTOREDISPLAY                                                                                                HEAD: RESTOREDISPLAY \ move picture from cache to display       T: OUTERSPACE 1 |DISPLAY T;                                                                                                     HEAD: PRESERVEDISPLAY \ move picture from display to cache      T: OUTERSPACE 0 |DISPLAY T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \ ESCDISABLE ESCENABLE OFFCACHE ONCACHE                                                                                         HEAD: ESCDISABLE                                                T: ( -- \ turn off escape key path to game options)               ESC-EN OFF T;                                                 HEAD: ESCENABLE                                                 T: ( -- \ turn on  escape key path to game options)               ESC-EN ON T;                                                                                                                  ( install number of cache blocks in variable [#cache] during)   ( configure-system)                                             HEAD: OFFCACHE ( -- \ turn cache memory off)                    T: #CACHE OFF AUTO-CACHE T;                                                                                                     HEAD: ONCACHE ( -- \ turn cache memory back on)                 T: [#CACHE] @ #CACHE ! AUTO-CACHE T;                            \ CHECKSUM NEWDOSMSGS ?INNERSPACE >RELATIVE                                                                                     HEAD: CHECKSUM ( addr count -- \ accum a check sum given)       T: ( memory start and byte count)                                 0 DO DUP I + C@ CKSUM +! 1 /LOOP DROP T;                                                                                      HEAD: NEWDOSMSGS                                                T: ' [ASKMOUNT] ASKMOUNT ! ' [VERSIONERROR] 'VERSIONERR ! T;                                                                    HEAD: ?INNERSPACE ( seg -- t )                                  T:  OUTERSPACE > NOT T;                                                                                                         HEAD: >RELATIVE ( seg -- seg' t )                               \ If seg in innerspace make relative to DS else make            \ relative to lfseg. 0=lfseg relative.                          T:  DUP ?INNERSPACE IF @DS - 1 ELSE LFSEG @ - 0 THEN T;         \ PUSHVECT POPVECT >ABSOLUTE                                                                                                    HEAD: >ABSOLUTE ( seg t -- seg' )                               \ Inverse of >RELATIVE.                                         T:  IF @DS + ELSE LFSEG @ + THEN T;                                                                                             HEAD: PUSHVECT ( -- nnnnnn \ push selected execution vectors)   T:  BUF-SEG @ DBUF-SEG @ =                                          BLTSEG @ >RELATIVE   3DSEG @ >RELATIVE                          #VECTORS 0 DO I VECTORS @ LOOP T;                                                                                           HEAD: POPVECT ( nnnnnn -- \ pop selected execution vectors)     T:  0 #VECTORS 1- DO I VECTORS ! -1 +LOOP                           >ABSOLUTE 3DSEG ! >ABSOLUTE BLTSEG !                            IF DBUF-SEG ELSE HBUF-SEG THEN @ BUF-SEG ! T;                                                                               \ .LOADING .LOADED                                                                                                              HEAD: .LOADING ( -- \ display message to user)                  T: ERASELINE                                                       " LOADING GAME IN PROGRESS..." .PAGE                            55  17 POS. ." PLEASE WAIT" >0FONT T;                                                                                        HEAD: .LOADED                                                   T: ( -- \ game load complete, wait for key then exit)              ERASELINE                                                       " ...GAME LOAD COMPLETE." .PAGE 1500 MS T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ .SAVING DONE                                                                                                                  HEAD: .SAVING ( -- \ display message to user)                   T: ERASELINE                                                       " SAVING GAME..." .PAGE                                         55  17 POS. ." PLEASE WAIT" >0FONT T;                                                                                        HEAD: DONE ( -- \ game save complete, wait for key then exit)   T: ERASELINE                                                      " GAME SAVE COMPLETE." .PAGE                                    PRESSEXIT T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ PRMSAV PRMLOD                                                 CREATE PRMSAV ( addr -- \ save parm stack image at addr)         ( with the parameter stack pointer in the format:)              ( [sp][---------1000 bytes--------]<-sp0)                       HERE DUP 2- !  HEX 5B C, 89 C, 27 C, 43 C, 43 C, 56 C, 57 C,    8B C, FB C, 8B C, 36 C, SP0 , 81 C, EE C, E8 C, 03 C, B9 C,     E8 C, 03 C, F3 C, A4 C, 5F C, 5E C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C,     27 C,                                                          CREATE PRMLOD ( addr -- \ given addr of parm stack image)         ( move it to the stack area and load the parm stack pointer)   HERE DUP 2- ! 5B C, 8B C, 27 C, 43 C, 43 C, 89 C, 76 C, FE C,   89 C, 7E C, FC C, 8B C, F3 C, FA C, 1E C, 07 C,                                               8B C, 3E C, SP0 , 81 C, EF C,     E8 C, 03 C, B9 C, E8 C, 03 C, F3 C, A4 C, 03 C, 26 C, ' SDROP , 8B C, 76 C, FE C, 8B C, 7E C, FC C, FB C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C,     FF C, 27 C, DECIMAL                                            \ RETSAV RETJMP                                                 HEX                                                             CREATE RETSAV ( addr -- \ save return stack image at addr)       ( with the current return stack pointer in the format:)         ( [rp][--------220 bytes--------]<-r0) HERE DUP 2- !            5B C, 89 C, 2F C, 43 C, 43 C, 56 C, 57 C, 8B C, FB C, 8B C,     36 C, R0 , 81 C, EE C, DC C, 00 C, B9 C, DC C, 00 C, F3 C,      A4 C, 5F C, 5E C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                CREATE RETJMP ( addr -- \ given addr of return stack image)       ( move it to the return stack and jump to next word)            HERE DUP 2- ! FA C, 1E C, 07 C,                                 5B C, 8B C, 2F C, 43 C, 43 C, 8B C, F3 C, 57 C, 8B C, 3E C,     R0 , 81 C, EF C, DC C, 00 C, B9 C, DC C, 00 C, F3 C, A4 C,      5F C, 03 C, 2E C, ' RDROP , 8B C, 76 C, 00 C, 45 C, 45 C,       FB C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                           DECIMAL                                                         \ .RS testing words                                             exit                                                            V= RBASE                                                        V= R0'                                                          V= RP'                                                          : .RS ( addr -- \ dump return stack image names at addr)          DUP RBASE !                                                     DUP 82 + R0' !                                                  R0 @ SWAP @ - R0' @ SWAP - RP' !                                BEGIN                                                             RP' @ R0' @ = NOT                                             WHILE                                                             RP' @ @  2 RP' +!                                               2- @ 2+ NFA CR ID.                                            REPEAT ;                                                                                                                      \ |DISK                                                         HEAD: |DISK ( mem-seg mem-offset base-blk #bytes tf -- \)       T: ( move data to/from memory to disk, tf=1-->disk )              >R DUP 0 1024 U/MOD ( mseg moff bblk #b rem blks -- tf)         SWAP IF 1+ THEN     ( mseg moff bblk #b blks' -- tf)            ?DUP IF 0 DO                                                              4 PICK I 64 * +  4 PICK                                         @DS 5 PICK I + BLOCK 2OVER 2OVER                                J NOT ?2SWAP                                                    9 PICK 1K UMIN LCMOVE                                           J IF UPDATE THEN                                                5 PICK 1K UMIN CHECKSUM                                         DROP 2DROP 1024 -                                               LOOP                                                          I IF SAVE-BUFFERS THEN                                       THEN R> DROP 2DROP 2DROP T;                              \ <DISK >DISK                                                                                                                   HEAD: <DISK                                                     T: ( mem-seg mem-offset base-blk #bytes -- \ move data)            ( from disk to memory)                                          0 |DISK T;                                                                                                                   HEAD: >DISK                                                     T: ( mem-seg mem-offset base-blk #bytes -- \ move data)            ( from memory to disk)                                          1 |DISK T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ ARR>DISK  DISK>ARR  ARRAYSPACESIZE                            HEAD: ARB ( -- array-base-seg )                                 \ Don't include music in save/load.                             t: LFSEG @ 50 + T;                                              HEAD: ARRAYSPACE ( -- bytes )                                   T: SYSK @ 64 * 1- arb - 16*   ( seg off blk #bytes --) T;                                                                       HEAD: ARR>DISK ( -- \ move array image to save disk)            T: arb 0 ARRBLK                                                    ARRAYSPACE                 ( seg off blk #bytes --)             >DISK T;                                                                                                                     HEAD: DISK>ARR ( -- \ load array image from save disk)          T: arb 0 ARRBLK                                                    ARRAYSPACE                 ( seg off blk #bytes --)             <DISK T;                                                     \ DSP>DISK  DISK>DSP                                                                                                            HEAD: DSP>DISK ( -- \ move display image from temporary )       T: ( location in cache to save disk)                               OUTERSPACE 0 DSPBLK  16K >DISK T;                                                                                                                                                            HEAD: DISK>DSP ( -- \ move display image from save disk to )    T: ( temporary location in cache)                                  OUTERSPACE 0 DSPBLK  16K <DISK T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ DISK>KRN KRN>DISK KERNSAVESTART                                                                                               HEAD: KERNSAVESIZE ( -- bytes )                                 T: OVA @ KERNSAVESTART - T;                                                                                                     HEAD: DISK>KRN ( -- \ move kernal thru OVA from save disk)      T: @DS KERNSAVESTART KRNBLK  KERNSAVESIZE <DISK T;                                                                              HEAD: KRN>DISK ( -- \ move kernal thru OVA to save disk)        T: @DS KERNSAVESTART KRNBLK  KERNSAVESIZE >DISK T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \ RTN>DISK  DISK>RTN  PRM>DISK  DISK>PRM                                                                                        HEAD: RTN>DISK ( -- \ save return stack to disk)                T: RTNBLK BLOCK RETSAV UPDATE T;                                                                                                HEAD: DISK>RTN                                                  T: ( -- \ get return stack from disk and move it to)               ( return stack temp array)                                      RTNBLK BLOCK RTNTEMP 222 CMOVE T;                                                                                            HEAD: PRM>DISK ( -- \ save parm stack to disk)                  T: PRMBLK BLOCK PRMSAV UPDATE T;                                                                                                HEAD: DISK>PRM ( -- \ get parm stack from disk)                 T: PRMBLK BLOCK PRMLOD T;                                                                                                       \ DATASAVE                                                                                                                      HEAD: DATASAVE ( -- \ save game image data to disk)             T: .SAVING           \ give user message                           CKSUM OFF         \ initialize checksum                         (restore)                                                       KRN>DISK          \ save kernal thru ova                        DSP>DISK          \ save display image                          ARR>DISK          \ save data arrays to disk                    PRM>DISK          \ save parameter stack to disk                RTN>DISK          \ save return stack to disk                   CKSUM @ :CKSUM !  \ save checksum                               SAVE-BUFFERS T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \ SETSAVE CLRSAVE @HOST !HOST                                   HEAD: !:SAVE ( n -- \ set game-saved flag)                      T: :SAVE ! T;                                                   HEAD: SETSAVE ( & timestamp;leaves stara mounted)               T: TS@ STS TS@ :ts! 1 !:save SWAP TS!                              MOUNTA :TS! 1 !:save ts! save-buffers t;                                                                                     HEAD: CLRSAVE ( -- \ clear game-saved flag)                     T: 0 !:SAVE MOUNTB 0 !:SAVE SAVE-BUFFERS T;                     HEAD: @HOST ( -- nnnnnn )                                       \ Get current host environment parameters from kernel.          T:  HOST-ENTRIES 0 DO I HOST @ LOOP (RESTORE) T;                HEAD: !HOST ( nnnnnn -- )                                       \ Set host environment parameters for kernel.                   T:  0 HOST-ENTRIES 1- DO I HOST ! -1 +LOOP CFIGARRAYS               (SETUP) ' initmus module mounta T;                          \ DATALOAD                                                      HEAD: DATALOAD ( -- \ load game image data to memory)           T: .LOADING           \ give user message                          CKSUM OFF          \ initialize checksum                        EMPTY-BUFFERS                                                   @HOST              \ preserve new environment pointers          DISK>KRN           \ load kernal thru ova                       !HOST              \ resolve old kernal image to new environs   DISK>DSP           \ load display image                         DISK>ARR           \ load data arrays                           DISK>PRM           \ load parameter stack                       DISK>RTN           \ load return stack to RTNTEMP               CKSUM @ :CKSUM @ = \ cmp check sum                              IF   .LOADED                                                    ELSE .CKSUMERROR   \ error abort                                THEN T;                                                      \ LOAD.GAME                                                                                                                     : LOAD.GAME ( -- \ load game state from file A.)                  NEWDOSMSGS                     \ install dos message vectors    >DISPLAY DARK BORDER           \ draw border & logo             .LOADHEAD                      \ draw heading                   EMPTY-BUFFERS OFFCACHE                                          SAVECHK                        \ check if saved, err abort      MOUNTA                         \ load save disk                 DATALOAD                      